# Search overrides. VS Code (cmd+P and the search panel) and ripgrep read this
# file and give it precedence over .gitignore in the same directory. Git itself
# never reads it, so nothing here changes what is tracked or committed.
#
# The root .gitignore hides /repos/*, /spaces/* and /docs/* from git - that
# content belongs to the service repos, or describes private incidents - and
# VS Code honours .gitignore everywhere, which hid them from search too. These
# negations put them back for *search* only. Every .gitignore *inside* a repo or
# worktree still applies underneath, so node_modules/, .next/, dist/ and vendor/
# stay out of the results.

!/repos/*
!/spaces/*
!/docs/*

# Release runbooks are small and worth searching; drop this line if not.
!/release/*

# Nothing under a repo's own .git needs indexing.
.git/
